  "interpretation": "Independent re-derivation of the Hansen 3-component chi reproduces the signed external-validation receipt exactly (max |err| 0.00e+00 chi units; MAE 0.6558, Pearson 0.8692), confirming the prefactor and Ra metric. Swapping ONLY the cohesive-distance term for the single Hildebrand parameter delta_total (Hildebrand & Scott 1950) degrades MAE from 0.6558 to 1.7298 chi units (2.64x worse) and Pearson from 0.869 to 0.460. The degradation is concentrated in the strongly hydrogen-bonding water systems (PVA, PEG, PS in water): Hansen MAE 1.224 vs Hildebrand MAE 4.266, because the scalar delta folds water's large delta_H=42.3 into a single term and grossly over-predicts chi. This a-priori, unfitted comparison corroborates Hansen's central thesis that resolving cohesive energy into dD/dP/dH is required for polar/H-bonding coating systems, and is not reproducible by the 1-D Hildebrand parameter.",
